{"name":"Balmy","hex":"#c5d8de","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"balmy","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Producing balm.","Soothing or fragrant."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/balmy"}],"entries":[{"title":"Coralie Balmy","blocks":[{"text":"Coralie Balmy is a French freestyle swimmer. Balmy was born in La Trinité, Martinique. She won her first senior title at the 2008 European Aquatics Championships in Eindhoven in the 4 × 200 m relay freestyle. At the same Championships she won the silver medal in the 400 m freestyle with the time of 4:04.15, all-time fourth fastest behind Federica Pellegrini's world record. At the 2008 Summer Olympics in Beijing, she finished fourth in the 400 m freestyle final. On 6 December 2008 she set the world record for the 200 m freestyle at the French National Championships in Angers, France in a time of 1:53.16. At the 2012 Summer Olympics her 4 × 200 m freestyle team won the bronze medal in a time of 7:47.49. The split times: Camille Muffat (1:55.51); Charlotte Bonnet (1:57.78); Ophélie-Cyrielle Étienne (1:58.05); Coralie Balmy (1:56.15)."},{"items":["Achievements","2007: SC European Championships\n3rd 200 m freestyle (1:54.43)","3rd 200 m freestyle (1:54.43)","2008: LC European Championships\n1st 4×200 m freestyle (7:52.09)\n2nd 400 m freestyle (4:04.15)","1st 4×200 m freestyle (7:52.09)","2nd 400 m freestyle (4:04.15)"]},{"items":["3rd 200 m freestyle (1:54.43)"]},{"items":["1st 4×200 m freestyle (7:52.09)","2nd 400 m freestyle (4:04.15)"]}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Coralie_Balmy_lors_des_Championnats_de_France_en_petit_bassin_2012.jpg/330px-Coralie_Balmy_lors_des_Championnats_de_France_en_petit_bassin_2012.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coralie_Balmy","wikidata":"Q271191"},{"title":"Jérémy Balmy","blocks":[{"text":"Jérémy Fabrice Balmy is a French professional footballer who plays as a forward for an amateur side AS Rousson."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/J%C3%A9r%C3%A9my_Balmy","wikidata":"Q16211921"}],"images":[],"sounds":{"balmy":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/94/En-au-balmy.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/9/94/En-au-balmy.ogg/En-au-balmy.ogg.mp3"}]},"pictures":[{"title":"Confederate Soldiers from the State of Georgia - Balmy, H C - 28th Infantry - DPLA - 026660fd1ee5616c10773a94f2b5f49a","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Confederate_Soldiers_from_the_State_of_Georgia_-_Balmy%2C_H_C_-_28th_Infantry_-_DPLA_-_026660fd1ee5616c10773a94f2b5f49a.jpg/500px-Confederate_Soldiers_from_the_State_of_Georgia_-_Balmy%2C_H_C_-_28th_Infantry_-_DPLA_-_026660fd1ee5616c10773a94f2b5f49a.jpg","ratio":0.4569789674952199,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Confederate_Soldiers_from_the_State_of_Georgia_-_Balmy,_H_C_-_28th_Infantry_-_DPLA_-_026660fd1ee5616c10773a94f2b5f49a.jpg","share":0.56875},{"title":"Grey heron (00129p)","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Grey_heron_%2800129p%29.jpg/500px-Grey_heron_%2800129p%29.jpg","ratio":0.8691693290734824,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Grey_heron_(00129p).jpg","share":0.565},{"title":"Steamer \"Majestic\" at Balmy Beach in Owen Sound, Ontario, Canada (1900) (5829828458)","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/Steamer_%22Majestic%22_at_Balmy_Beach_in_Owen_Sound%2C_Ontario%2C_Canada_%281900%29_%285829828458%29.jpg/500px-Steamer_%22Majestic%22_at_Balmy_Beach_in_Owen_Sound%2C_Ontario%2C_Canada_%281900%29_%285829828458%29.jpg","ratio":1.279749478079332,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Steamer_%22Majestic%22_at_Balmy_Beach_in_Owen_Sound,_Ontario,_Canada_(1900)_(5829828458)